  "rationale": "Block codeRepo:collection, mailClient:execution, and tokenCache:credentialAccess. Blocking mailClient prevents vpnSession and rdpLogin, which makes monitoringHost, hypervisor, and both routes to shareMount unreachable. Blocking tokenCache also prevents apiToken; with vpnSession unreachable, printServer and mailArchive are unreachable. Thus all four parents of the target are unreachable. At least three blocks are necessary because there are three internally disjoint sufficient attack routes: browserStore → fileServer → codeRepo; containerHost → tokenCache → printServer → mailArchive; and {sshKey, mailClient} → vpnSession → monitoringHost → dbReplica. Each route is supported directly by entry footholds and requires a separate block."
